❌ Camera AV Stream Management 2.7 (TC_AVSM_2_7.py)
   ↳ Test wrong assumption: step 27 escalates MaxFrameRate by +20 per maxConcurrentEncoders iteration (starting at minFrameRate+15) then again for the final exhaustion attempt, to force RESOURCE_EXHAUSTED; with maxConcurrentEncoders=1 that final attempt requests 65fps, which exceeds our declared VideoSensorParams.MaxFps (60) and is correctly rejected as DYNAMIC_CONSTRAINT_ERROR first, per Matter 1.6/1.5.1 §11.2.8.4.12's own Effect on Receipt order (unsupported-field checks precede the resource check). Any device with a finite MaxFps hits this same issue eventually — it's not specific to our declared value.
